---
lang: en
title: Unlock an article — “The Light-House Keeper of Aspinwall”
description: A free opening and a micropayment for the rest. The simplest GetViaMsg use case for publishers.
crumb: Publishers · Unlock an article
altUrl: /publisher/unlock-article/
gvm: true
permalink: /en/publisher/unlock-article/
---

{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}
{% from "gvm/payment-dialog.njk" import paymentDialog %}
{% from "gvm/paywall-inline.njk" import paywallInline %}

{% block content %}
<div class="container">
    <article class="article">
        <header class="article-head">
            <p class="kicker">Literary archive</p>
            <h1>{{ texts.latarnik.title.en }}</h1>
            <p class="byline">
                {{ texts.latarnik.author }} · {{ texts.latarnik.year }} · short
                story
            </p>
            <p class="lead">
                “The Light-House Keeper of Aspinwall” is one of Henryk
                Sienkiewicz’s best-known short stories — an old soldier takes a
                lighthouse keeper’s post after years of wandering. The opening
                paragraphs below are free; the rest unlocks with a single
                micropayment.
            </p>
        </header>

        {#
          The gated element. gvm.js reads `data-gvm-price` / `-reference` from
          here and hides everything after `data-gvm-hide-sections` sections,
          then injects the `paywall` template into `#article`.
        #}
        <div
            id="article"
            class="article-body wait-for-script"
            data-gvm-reference="latarnik-en"
            data-gvm-price="1.99"
            data-gvm-template-name="payment"
            data-gvm-hide-template-name="paywall"
            data-gvm-hide-strategy="hide"
            data-gvm-hide-sections="6"
            data-gvm-metadata-title="{{ texts.latarnik.title.en }}"
            data-gvm-category="article"
        >
            {% for paragraph in texts.latarnik.paras.en %}
            <p>{{ paragraph }}</p>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>

        <footer class="article-source">
            <p>
                Text: {{ texts.latarnik.author }}, “{{ texts.latarnik.title.en
                }}” ({{ texts.latarnik.year }}), translated by Jeremiah Curtin
                (1893) — public domain, source: {{ texts.latarnik.source.en }}.
                This is a GetViaMsg showcase of single-article sales; the text
                itself is unchanged.
            </p>
            <details>
                <summary>How it works (for developers)</summary>
                <p>
                    The full text is in the DOM, but gvm.js hides everything
                    after the sixth paragraph and injects the
                    <code>paywall</code> template where
                    <code>#article</code> is. Payment is handled by one shared
                    <code>payment</code> template that reads the amount and the
                    content reference from <code>data-gvm-*</code> attributes.
                </p>
            </details>
        </footer>
    </article>
</div>

{{ paymentDialog({ t: i18n[lang], termsUrl: site.termsUrl, termsVersion: site.termsVersion }) }}
{{ paywallInline({ t: i18n[lang], termsUrl: site.termsUrl }) }}
{% endblock %}
